From b08c8f95582958a8e9aa8c30f5d33555144c51d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:06:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(tools): one tool meridian for each mill kind, split
 into convex atoms

Add camcraft_tools::meridian: the cutting outline rho(z) of a mill as
lines and circular arcs (the SpunPoint form, one cutting flag for each
segment), Tool::meridian() for the end mill, ball, bull, drill, chamfer,
T-slot, keyseat, dovetail and lollipop, and Meridian::atoms(), which
splits it into convex solids of revolution: a frustum for a line, a
torus zone for a convex arc, chord frusta (outer bound) or tangent
frusta (inner bound) under a sag limit for a concave arc.

Degenerate input is refused by name (MeridianError). No consumer reads
the meridian yet.

A sim unit test pins that the atoms of each kind are the solids that
Cutter::atoms builds today, within 1e-9 mm.

Fixes #3367

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
